### ============================================================================
### Short-term memory (ChatMemory-backed, conversation id: testActor:testSession)
### ============================================================================

### STM — tell name
POST http://localhost:8080/api/short
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "My name is Andrei"
}

### STM — ask name
POST http://localhost:8080/api/short
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "What is my name?"
}

### ============================================================================
### Long-term memory (AgentCore Memory, persisted across sessions)
### ============================================================================

### LTM — tell name
POST http://localhost:8080/api/long
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "My name is Andrei"
}

### LTM — ask name
POST http://localhost:8080/api/long
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "What is my name?"
}

### LTM — write a fact (ingestion to LTM may take ~1 minute on the AWS side)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/long
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "My favorite color is green. Please remember this."
}

### LTM — recall the fact (run after giving AWS a minute to extract)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/long
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "What is my favorite color? One word."
}

### ============================================================================
### Conversation history (STM buffer inspection / reset)
### ============================================================================

### Get STM history
GET http://localhost:8080/api/history

### Clear STM history
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/history

### ============================================================================
### Diagnostics
### ============================================================================

### List wired-up LTM strategies (in retrieval order)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/ltm/strategies
